@startuml
' The fault -> error -> failure chain of Avizienis et al. (2004), applied to D1,
' with the dormancy and detection latency that made it expensive.
title D1 through the dependability chain — <latex>\textrm{fault} \to \textrm{error} \to \textrm{failure}</latex>\n<size:11>after Avizienis, Laprie, Randell & Landwehr (2004), DOI 10.1109/TDSC.2004.2</size>

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #455A64

skinparam activity {
  BorderThickness 1.5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  DiamondBorderColor #455A64
}

|#ECEFF1|Developer|
start
:**FAULT** — dormant
""onNodesChange([{type:"remove"}])""
in the delete-node menu action;
note right #FFF3E0
  A latent fault: correct-looking code that
  omits the framework's edge cascade.
  Dormant for as long as nobody deletes a
  node that has edges.
end note

|#FFF3E0|Author in the editor|
:**ACTIVATION** — delete a node
that has at least one edge;
:Edges survive their node;
if (does the UI show anything?) then (**no**)
  :React Flow silently skips
  an edge to a missing node;
  note right #FFEBEE
    The error is now present and
    **undetected**. This is the whole
    incident in one step.
  end note
else (yes)
  :author repairs it — never happened;
  stop
endif

|#FFEBEE|Persistence|
:**ERROR** committed
graphl with <latex>\exists (u,v) \in E,\; u \notin V</latex>;
:Every reopen re-materialises it;
:Every save rewrites it;
note right #FFEBEE
  Error is now **self-sustaining**, so the
  team is permanently undeployable — the
  step that turned a slip into an outage.
end note

|#E3F2FD|embers backend|
:**FAILURE** — deploy rejected
""node <id> is missing context"";
note right #FFF3E0
  Detection latency: the fault was
  introduced in one process and detected
  in another, after two saves and a
  deploy. Diagnosis needed a byte-level
  comparison of contexts against vertex
  ids to even locate it.
end note

|#E8F5E9|After the fix|
:Fault removed — delegate to ""deleteElements"";
:Error unrepresentable — save filters;
:Existing errors repaired — load filters;
:Reverting the fixes fails 10 of 13 D1 tests
and 6 of 15 render tests (§8);
stop

legend right
  |= band |= meaning |
  |<#ECEFF1>| where the fault was written |
  |<#FFF3E0>| silent / unobserved |
  |<#FFEBEE>| error present and spreading |
  |<#E3F2FD>| where failure finally surfaced |
  |<#E8F5E9>| post-fix state |
endlegend
@enduml
